            <ArticleTitle>Late rejection after transabdominal pre-peritoneal inguinal repair: laparoscopic extraction of mesh.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 29-year-old man who developed mesh rejection 3 years after laparoscopic transabdominal pre-peritoneal inguinal repair. The mesh, which was lying in a fluid cavity adherent to the urinary bladder and right iliac vessel, was removed laparoscopically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
